<title>CHINA: China Jan-Sept gold output 84.6 tonnes - paper.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Sept gold output 84.6 tonnes - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>China produced 84.6 tonnes of gold in the first nine months of this year, up 13.3 percent from the same period of 1995, the Futures Herald said.</p>
<p>Gold output in September alone was 11.8 tonnes, according to an edition of the newspaper seen in Beijing on Sunday.  </p>
<p>The newspaper did not give a comparative figure for September alone.</p>
<p>It said that output in the first nine months of the year represented 91.9 percent of the target for all of 1996.</p>
<p>The latest figures showed production was maintaining its fairly high growth rate, the newspaper said. It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
